* Intent

Turn registry loading into a functional fold over a declared list of *packages*,
and settle the repo's package distribution + the four run scenarios BEFORE any
loader change. The unifying idea: *=registry= is not a thing, =package= is.*

The supply is FOUR in-tree packages (beef, verbatim: *"core call vivalence -
services and such. education is education. playground check. add another for
testing called simulation."*):

| package     | holds                                                          |
|-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------|
| @vivalence  | platform services: datamap, hallucinator, lighthouse, nlp      |
| @education  | the domain: corpus/ontology/domain kernels + game/tactic/teacher/homepage/dashboard modes |
| @development | dev/demo modes, type =playground= (spawner, card, dealer, automaton, switchboard, spawned) |
| @simulation | the testing world: the test variant (daemons/services inlined, no circuitry indirection) + future fixtures |

And the identity axis is RENAMED (beef, verbatim: *"the package name is now the
owner name … we need to rename this variable owner. I think package is the more
accurate term."*): =owner= → =package= throughout — manifest field, pensieve top
axis, =cast.lookup=, =is.lookup=. Free disambiguation win: =owner= stays
available for the datamap's user-scoped ENTITY owner (different concept, same
word today).

Reference ripple (beef: *"the things now don't need to only reference @vivalence
but also all of the other package names"*): every module lookup string re-homes
to its package — =@vivalence/game/write= → =@education/game/write=.

Testament dissolves as a package and survives as the machine's RUN SURFACE
(beef: *"the testament is the thing that we run live … the running files"* +
*"We might want to move the circuitry for that package, like the package as a
whole, into the registry"* — judged YES for the authored half): the authored
variant (test.viva.js + environment jsonc) moves into
=registry/simulation/variant/=; the derived half (system locks/logs, mountpoint
dbs, .env, secrets) stays gitignored under =testament/=. **The gitignore line
becomes the authored/derived line** — same axis as variant-declares /
ledger-pins.

*NO circuitry indirection* (beef, addendum: *"let's lose the circuitry
terminology entirely. Our variant modules don't export any circuitry.
Paladin doesn't handle circuitry. They just export runtime services daemons,
such stuff."*): a variant module exports =daemons=/=services=/=runtime=/=clients=
DIRECTLY — no separate =circuitry.js= file, no =export * as circuitry from
"./circuitry.js"= re-export, no =cake.circuitry?.X= merge in =variant.js=.
Two live files carried this pattern — both get inlined, not moved alongside:
=testament/variant/circuitry.js= (daemons: brazilian + playground) into
=test.viva.js=; =registry/wafers/@vivalence/variant/multiplayer/circuitry.js=
(daemons: brazilian) into =multiplayer.viva.js=. =localhost.viva.js= never
had this indirection — its daemon was always inline. Content-drift NOTE
(not reconciled, just surfaced): multiplayer's brazilian daemon config and
testament's have diverged — multiplayer lacks =game/riddler=/=game/nyan=,
carries =tactic/five-fold-session=+=tactic/clinic=+=dashboard/dataspace=
UNCOMMENTED where testament has them commented out. Inlining preserves each
as-is; unifying them is a separate, unrequested call.

This quest resolves the *in-tree* case. Out-of-tree apparatus (ledger,
materialize, =viva install package=) stays deferred.

** The locked design (the decision trail)

*** package = identity (was: owner)
=pensieve= keys =package→type→slug→version=. =@vivalence= is the core PLATFORM
package, not "the org". Two packages shipping =game/flashcard= land under
different package keys → no collision.

**** DERIVED by default, LOCKED on demand (beef, addendum)
The package source is computed *within =vip.mount='s own scope* — a package
needn't author =package: "@vivalence"= at all; the name derives from the
mount path (=registry/vivalence= → =@vivalence=). No mode/kernel/service
needs to export =manifest.package= either — a module inherits whatever its
mount stamped, by default.

A =package.viva.js= (or any module) MAY still self-declare =manifest.package=
to *lock* an explicit identity — the self-declaration wins over the
mount-derived default when present. This is opt-in, not required: one fixture
inside =@simulation= (=scenario/lock-demo=) exercises the lock path and
doubles as the living doc for it — see tangle below.

Reserved-word wrinkle: =package= is a strict-mode reserved word — =const
{ package } = manifest= is a SyntaxError in modules. Convention: object KEYS
stay =package= (property access is legal); local BINDINGS are named
=packageName=. Never destructure the bare word.

*** supply / demand — unchanged
system = supply (fills the pensieve, pre-variant). variant = demand (composes
module identities). Runtime stays package-blind (=accio= never knows a package
exists); the variant is package-aware.

*** variant declares, ledger pins — unchanged (flake.nix / flake.lock)
=variant.packages= is the authored declaration; the per-machine ledger stays
deferred (in-tree: source = mount, version = working copy — a ledger is a
tautology).

*** the four scenarios (the settlement)
| scenario      | packages                        | variant mount                          | state (derived)                | env |
|---------------+---------------------------------+----------------------------------------+--------------------------------+-----|
| development   | all four                        | =registry/simulation/variant= (tracked) | =testament/{system,mountpoint}= | =testament/.env= (machine-local; template =.env.example=) |
| testing       | all four (scenarios mount packages) | same tracked variant — fresh clone + CI now possible | temp / =testament/=            | same =--env-file=; secrets via env |
| docker        | image COPYs =registry/= → all four baked, VARIANT INCLUDED | =/viva/repository/registry/simulation/variant= (11.4 wires it) | container volume ≙ testament   | injected ENV |
| local install | =viva install variant= → =~/.viva= | installed copy                         | =~/.viva=                      | =~/.viva= |

The standing bug this kills: =deno task runtime/test= reads
=--env-file=../../testament/.env= AND the test variant sat gitignored — the
suite depended on untracked files. After 11.0 the variant + environment jsonc
are tracked; only mounts/secrets stay machine-local.

@education's own shipped variants (brazilian, spanish) are DEFERRED — the dev/
test world lives in @simulation for now; education variants land when the
spanish daemon revives.

*** deno static-import resolution is already solved (no S0)
=@vivalence/*= JS import specifiers resolve by *workspace member name*
(location-independent) and are a DIFFERENT namespace from lookup strings — the
rename touches lookup strings only, never import statements. Spawns already
pass =--config <root>=.

*** the boot order is already correct
=runtime/run.js= =variant.mount()= precedes =die.js= =registry()=. No reorder.

